{
  "name": "core-declarative",
  "description": "The declarative vocabulary (D103's step 5) over test.Votes, a behavior whose declaration states its rules and which no Rust implements (runtime/engine/testdata/rules/declarations/test.Votes.behavior.json): a vote that upserts the caller's row of a sub-table, its parameter held to 1 to the config's maxScore; fields derived from the rows as a count, a sum, an average, a highest, a lowest and a filtered count; guards over the row's fields, the Workflow's status and the caller compared with a field that holds a subject; a counter an operation adjusts; an operation that moves the Workflow; two reactions heard from the change queue; the owner kept as its create gave it and a title an accepted row freezes, in Constants' and StateRules' words; and the define refusals. Cases written by hand in the recorded format, since no engine implements a declarative behavior. Each answer holds what the replayer compares: a record's id, data and behaviors, an operation's result, and a refusal whole, in the core's words; what only the engine's store answers (sequence numbers, versions, timestamps, the document a define echoes) is left out.",
  "source": "written by hand (D103's step 5): runtime/engine/testdata/rules/scenarios/core-declarative.json",
